{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths","answer":"Verified in SCOPe release 2.08: d2kq5a_ (sunid 264989), d3v6pa_ (sunid 265556), and d4cj9a_ (sunid 265996) share the full lineage a (All alpha proteins) > a.298 (Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix) > a.298.1 (TAL effector-like superfamily) > a.298.1.1 (TAL effector family). Their genetic SEQRES domain sequences are 51, 373, and 752 residues, so the length difference is real.

Why the length difference does not split the family: SCOPe's family placement rests on a shared tandem repeat unit, not on total length or repeat count. The family repeat annotation is 4cj9 A:259-292, attached to the canonical representative d4cj9a_. The records explicitly handle repeat-count variation with a heterogeneity flag: d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ each carry an 're' inconsistency entry reading 'applies to all domains of a family if the common domain is composed of a different number of small repeating units'. d2kq5a_ also carries a 'single repeat' comment, consistent with its 51-residue length. In the sequence text, d3v6pa_ and d4cj9a_ visibly contain many tandem copies of a repeated motif (for example, the recurring '...LPVLCQAHGLTP...' and '...GGKQALE...'-type units). The length difference therefore reflects how many copies of the common unit a domain contains, and SCOPe records this as a family-wide heterogeneity note rather than as grounds for separate families. Homology is marked as implied by the family level (homology_scope px) for all three domains, with no homology warnings returned.

Limits: (1) The repeat coordinates 259-292 belong to the canonical 4cj9 A representative. The API states they do not apply to the requested node for d2kq5a_ or d3v6pa_ (coordinates_apply_to_requested_node is false), so I cannot map that range onto their residues, and I did not run a sequence alignment to locate repeats in them. I have not verified their exact repeat counts or domain boundaries. (2) The family placement is SCOPe's positive assertion of close relationship; I did not retrieve sequence or structure hits, so I cannot quantify identity between the three domains from this evidence. (3) Family placement does not establish DNA-binding specificity, repeat-variable residue content, or any function for these particular domains; the DNA-recognition role of TAL effectors is general pretrained background, not something these records state. (4) The d4cj9a_ comment text ('complexed with se') is truncated in the response and I did not interpret it. (5) The species entries (Xanthomonas, Burkholderia rhizoxinica) are SCOPe hierarchy labels, not external taxonomy claims. (6) I did not compare historical releases, so no reclassification history is asserted.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_sequence","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/homology","/api/v1/sequences/sids/d2kq5a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json","/api/v1/sequences/sids/d3v6pa_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json","/api/v1/sequences/sids/d4cj9a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json","scop-homology/SKILL.md"]}]}
